\id EXA exotic corpus fixture — poetry, footnotes, lists, aligned words
\usfm 3.0
\ide UTF-8
\h Exotic A
\toc1 Exotic Sample A
\toc2 Exotic A
\toc3 ExA
\mt1 Exotic Sample A
\c 1
\s Prose with footnotes
\p
\v 1 The first verse carries a footnote \f + \fr 1:1 \ft Some manuscripts read \fqa another word\fqa* here. \f* inside its body.
\v 2 The second verse has a keyword footnote \f + \fr 1:2 \fk covenant \ft The term \+w covenant|x-occurrence="1" x-occurrences="1"\+w* is explained elsewhere. \f* and continues after it.
\v 3 \zaln-s |x-strong="G39720" x-lemma="Παῦλος" x-morph="Gr,N,,,,,NMS," x-occurrence="1" x-occurrences="1" x-content="Παῦλος"\*\w Paul|x-occurrence="1" x-occurrences="1"\w*\zaln-e\*
\zaln-s |x-strong="G14010" x-lemma="δοῦλος" x-morph="Gr,N,,,,,NMS," x-occurrence="1" x-occurrences="1" x-content="δοῦλος"\*\w a|x-occurrence="1" x-occurrences="1"\w*
\w servant|x-occurrence="1" x-occurrences="1"\w*\zaln-e\*, with a footnote \f + \fr 1:3 \ft An aligned verse can carry a footnote too. \f* after the milestone.
\s Poetry
\b
\q1
\v 4-5 Sing the first line of the song,
\q2 and answer with the second line;
\q1 lift the third line higher still,
\q2 and let the fourth line rest. \f + \fr 1:4 \ft The song is one span verse. \f*
\b
\d A quiet title between the songs
\q1
\v 6 One more line stands alone.
\c 2
\s Lists and late prose
\p
\v 1 Before the list there is prose.
\lh
\v 2 The list has these members:
\li1 the first member,
\li2 a nested member,
\li1 the last member.
\lf The list ends here.
\p
\v 3 After the list the prose returns, and the book ends.
